// Where the sandbox's characters may be: the `bodies_in_world` invariant halts the game when
// one ends a tick elsewhere. Inside means over a piece of what the built layouts have: each
// solid, ramp and volume counts by its own rectangle on the ground, not by the layout's
// bounding box, so the void beside the arena's corridor and beside the course's lane is
// outside (past `margin` of the pieces). The pieces: the arena's floor and walls (x and z
// -21.5..21.5), its corridor (x 21.5..44, z -5.5..5.5), the course's lane (x 44..86,
// z -5.5..5.5) and the canyon floor under the glide (x 86..141.5, z -17.5..17.5). Or over the
// loaded region's cells (the wilds: x -64..64, z 48..176; the region stays one rectangle;
// the voxel arena: x -128..128, z -528..-272, and its sea, `past_grid`, 100 m beyond).
// `margin` meters wider on every rectangle, and above `fall_below` (the canyon floor under
// the course's cliff is at -10, and so is the voxel arena's sea floor).
{
    "world": (
        margin: 4.0,
        fall_below: -30.0,
        past_grid: {"voxel_arena": 100.0},
    ),
}
